    "Matrix Chain Multiplication — Core Intuition\n",
    "Matrix multiplication cost depends on dimensions.\n",
    "If:\n",
    "(a xb )⋅(b×c)\n",
    "then:\n",
    "result size =\n",
    "a×c\n",
    "multiplication cost =\n",
    "a×b×c\n",
    "Why cost varies\n",
    "Different parenthesization creates different intermediate matrices.\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "(A1 × A2) × A3\n",
    "vs\n",
    "A1 × (A2 × A3)\n",
    "Both give same final matrix.\n",
    "But intermediate matrix dimensions differ.\n",
    "Those dimensions affect future multiplication costs.\n",
    "Core Goal\n",
    "Avoid expensive intermediate matrices.\n",
    "DP Pattern\n",
    "For every range:\n",
    "i → j\n",
    "try every split:\n",
    "k\n",
    "and compute:\n",
    "left_cost + right_cost + merge_cost\n",
    "Take minimum.\n",
    "Main Interview Insight\n",
    "MCM teaches:\n",
    "Interval DP\n",
    "Partition DP\n",
    "“Try all split points” pattern\n",
    "Used in problems like:\n",
    "Burst Balloons\n",
    "Boolean Parenthesization\n",
    "Merge Stones\n",
    "Palindrome Partitioning II"
   ]
